1 OCCU London Merchant and Banker. Arbuthnot Latham & Co, Arbuthnot Latham Bank. Govenor of the Bank of England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A London Merchant and Banker. Arbuthnot Latham & Co, Arbuthnot Latham Bank Director of the Bank of England 1838-1859. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfred Latham formed part of the intertwining of the Latham and Pulsford families. Alfred's father Thomas was in business with the Pulsford family as wine merchants in the 1790s and the will of Thomas Latham (1744-1818), dated 11/
2 CONC 06/1818, mentions Robert Pulsford and [his son] William Pulsford. In 1833 Alfred Latham married Frances Pulsford of Wimpole Street and Linslade Manor Bucks, the daughter of William Pulsford the elder and sister of William Pulsford
2 CONC  the younger and Robert Pulsford the younger (each of whom q.v). Alfred Latham was executor of the wills of both Robert Pulsford the elder and his son (Alfred's father-in-law) William Pulsford the elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arbuthnot Latham was primarily oriented towards India and Asia trade, but David Lascelles history of Arbuthnot Latham, published in 2013, is candid that 'Latham and Pulsford...made their fortunes not from their wine business but f
2 CONC rom managing sugar plantations in the West Indies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deputy Governor of the Bank of England 1859-1861. Governor of the Bank of England 1861-1863. Director of the Bank of England 1863-1878.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shown as owning Hamilton estate in Nevis 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wealth at death: £191,020 13S 1D Occupation: Merchant and Banker Associated Claims (2): Jamaica St Thomas-in-the-East, Surrey 192 (Sunning Hill Estate) £2,921 16S 0D Awardee (Executor or executrix): Tobago 27 (Orange Valley) £952 
2 CONC 1S 6D Awardee (Executor or executrix): Legacies Summary
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment Wilts, Somerset and Weymouth [1845203] £10000  Name partner: Arbuthnot Latham East India Merchant  
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence in 1836: Montague Place, Great St Helens Residence in 1841: Star & Garter Hotel, Petersham, Surrey (3 children at 23 Norfolk Street, Middlesex) Residence in 1851: 23 Norfolk Street, Hanover Square, Middlesex Residence in
2 CONC  1861: 23 Norfolk Street, London Residence in 1871: 23 Norfolk Street, Hanover Square, Middlesex Residence in 1881: 23 Norfolk Street, Hanover Square, Middlesex Death registered by Morton Latham (son)
2 CONT
2 CONT Executors of  Will: Morton Latham, William Latham & Charles Latham Gross Value of Estate: Â£191,620 (£17,215,315 in today's value http://www.moneysorter.co.uk/calculator_inflation.html 2011).
