1 NOTE {geni:about_me} TRINITY  COLLEGE  ADMISSIONS 51 http://brittlebooks.library.illinois.edu/brittlebooks_open/Books2009-06/trinco0001admtri/trinco0001admtriv00005/trinco0001admtriv00005_ocr.txt Latham, George. Son of Alfred Latham. B
2 CONC orn in London. School, Harrow (Dr Vaughan). Age 19. Pensioner, July 12, 1853. Tutor, Mr Cooper.   [Matriculated, 1854; B.A. 1858.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Resided in Ifield, near Crawley, Sussex.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following graduation from Trinity College, Cambridge George commenced work with his father's Merchant Bank ; Arbuthnot Latham in 1856 aged 25.  His father, Alfred Latham elected to retire on the 31 December 1865 ( along with Archy
2 CONC  Arbuthnot). In 1864 and 1865, the last two years of the US Civil War the partners had earned Pounds 69,000 (more than Pounds Four Million, Six Hundred Thousand today). Alfred Latham continued as a Director of The Bank of England 
2 CONC till 1878. George Latham was made Partner of Arbuthnot Latham in January, 1866 at the age of 31years with a 25% share of the Bank along with Hugh Gough Arbuthnot aged 26 years with 25%. They joined Senior Partner John Arbuthnot ag
2 CONC ed 63 years. George Latham died prematurely at the age of only 36 years on 25 June, 1871. His two sons; George Nix Latham aged 10 years and Frederick Nix Latham aged 6 years were either attending or still to attend school ( @ Char
2 CONC terhouse School, Goldalming ). George Latham's early death marked the end of the Latham Partnership at Arbuthnot Latham Bank. George's nephew; Stephen Latham, son of his brother William Latham (?) later worked at Arbuthnot Latham,
2 CONC  but did not became a partner.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT George was born September 7, 1835. The eldest child of Alfred Latham and Frances (Pulsford) Latham. I assume he was born at home at 23 Norfolk St., London ( Between The Strand and River Thames - near to Temple Station now) in the 
2 CONC family home (?).He was educated at Harrow School till June, 1853. He then attended Trinity College, Cambridge and matriculated in 1858 with a BA. All Alfred's boys had this education. George Latham worked at Arbuthnot Latham, his 
2 CONC fathers Merchant and Investment Bank in London from 1859 (?). On the 21 February 1860 George married Julia Louise Nix.  Their first child; George Nix Latham was born 23 December, 1860. Second child; Julia Frances Latham was born i
2 CONC n 1862. And third and final child, Frederick Nix Latham was born August 23, 1864 - the year before his father took over as Partner at Arbuthnot Latham Bank. In December, 1865 his father Alfred Latham elected to retire from Arbuthn
2 CONC ot Latham Bank and his son George was made Partner of the Bank with 25% equity. At the same time Archy Arbuthnot retired from the bank and made his son; Hugh Gough Arbuthnot Partner in his place with 25% equity. John Arbuthnot ret
2 CONC ained the other 50% equity and remained in the firm till his death in 1875 and lived at 69 Eaton Square and the country estate "Coworth Park" at Old Windsor, Berkshire. George Lastham was 31 years old when he took over the partner
2 CONC ship from his father. Alfred, his father continued as a Director of The Bank of England. After less than 6 years as Partner at Arbuthnot Latham, George Latham died prematurely in June, 1871 aged 36 years His sons; George Nix and F
2 CONC rederick Nix were at Charterhouse School, Goldalming and too young to get involved with the family bank. Alfred, the father of George lived another 14 years and died in 1885 at Hanover Square at the home of William Latham QC, his 
2 CONC son. His estate of Pounds 191,000 today would be worth 14 Million pounds.  
