1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frederick Nix Latham was the third child of George Latham and Julia Louise (Nix) Latham. His father George died prematurely at the age of 36 years, when Frederick was only 6 years old. He was educated at Charterhou
2 CONC se School, Goldalming, Surry from 1878 - 1882.  His brother George Nix Latham attended Trinity College, Cambridge.  Frederick studied Civil Engeineering at (?) University. He worked in finance as accountant / broker / banker (?) a
2 CONC nd possible with N.M. Rothchild for a short time and was retired by 1901 census. He married Marion Stonham (04/14/1861 to 04/06/1935) in 1885. Their first child; Violet Marion Latham was born 06/12/1887 ( died Melbourne, Australia
2 CONC  05/02/1970). Their second child; Leslie Frederick Latham was born 03/17/1889 (died Narrabri, N.W. NSW, Australia 05/06/1963) Frederick Nix Latham lived his early adult life at Greenwich, London. On retiring the family moved from 
2 CONC London to Southsea, Portsmouth before moving to Flushing, Foulmouth, Cornwall aproximatly 1908. His principal recreation was sailing and travel. It was said he was a member of the Royal Ocean Racing Club, Cowes Clubhouse. He joine
2 CONC d the Royal Cornwall Yacht Club in 1908 and owned two yachts; a 9 ton Auxiliary Yl named "Albion" and a 3 ton yawl named "Vioma". He traveled regularly to South America and to Australia, where his two children had moved to live. A
2 CONC fter the death of his first wife Marion in 1935, he moved  back to Southsea; to 9 Palmerston Court, Clarence Parade, Southsea, in the County of Southampton where the house was bombed during WW2. He married his carer, Violet Beryl 
2 CONC Burnand,{ born 09/09/1903 (?) and died 04/12/1974}. They married before the war we think on 09/09/1935 (?). He died at the age of 90 years at  Southsea, Portsmouth. Hi last will dated 3 December, 1953 was lodged with Markby, Stewa
2 CONC rt & Wadesons - Solicitors, 5 Bishopsgate, London, EC2. He appointed Lancelot Claude Bullock, Solicitor as Executor and Arthur Charles West of Winton House, Portsdown Hill Road, Cosham, Portsmouth and Violet Beryl Latham as Execut
2 CONC ors.     
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Nix Latham was the third child of George Latham and Julia Louise (Nix) Latham. His father George died prematurely at the age of 36 years, when Frederick was only 6 years old. George Latham held 25% of Arbuthnot Latham Me
2 CONC rchant and Investment Bank, gifted by his father Alfred Latham who jointly started the bank.  He was educated at Charterhouse School, Goldalming, Surrey from Oration Quarter, 1878  until the Long Quarter, 1880. He boarded at Robin
2 CONC ites boarding house. His brother, George Nix Latham attended the same Charterhouse School from 1875 to 1878 and later studied at Trinity College, Cambridge after Charterhouse School . Frederick Nix Latham studied Engineering and b
2 CONC ecame a Civil Engineer (University unknown). We think he worked in finance as an accountant / broker / banker (?) and possibly with N.M. Rothchild's (?).  He married Marion Stonham (04/14/1861 to 04/06/1935) in approximately 1885.
2 CONC  Their first child; Violet Marion Latham was born 06/12/1887 (died Melbourne, Australia 05/02/1970). Their second child; Leslie Frederick Latham was born 03/17/1889 (died Narrabri NSW, Australia 05/06/1963. Frederick Nix Latham li
2 CONC ved his early adult life in Greenwich, London. His principal recreation was sailing and travel. It was said he was a member of the Royal Ocean Racing Club, Ltd  Cowes for several years (?).  Frederick Nix Latham retired early and 
2 CONC moved first from London to Southsea, Portsmouth and later to Flushing, Falmouth, Cornwall in 1907 or 1908. He joined the Royal Cornwall Yacht Club in 1908 and owned two yachts; a 9 ton auxiliary Yl named "Albion" and a 3 ton yawl 
2 CONC named "Vioma". He traveled regularly to South America and to Australia, where his two children had moved to live. Later in life, after the death of his first wife Marion, in 1935, he moved back to Southsea to 9 Palmerston Court, C
2 CONC larence Parade, Southsea, in the County of Southampton where the house was bombed in WW2. He married for a second time to Violet Beryl Burnand ( born we estimate 09/09/1903 (?) and she died 04/12/1974. They married before the WW2 
2 CONC , soon after the death of Marion, we believe (09/09/1935 ?). Frederick Nix Latham died on 15th February, 1955 aged 90 years at Southsea, His last will dated 3 December, 1953 was lodged with Markby, Stewart, Wadesons - Solicitors, 
2 CONC 5 Bishopsgate , London EC2. He appointed Lancelot Claude Bullock, Solicitor as Attorney along with Arthur Charles West of West of Winton House, Portsdown, Hill Road, Cosham, Portsmouth and wife Violet Beryl Latham as Executors of 
2 CONC estate.    
