1 NAME Thomas /Latham/
2 GIVN Thomas
2 _MARNM Latham
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 DEC 1719
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 STAE Greater London
3 CTRY UK
1 DEAT
2 DATE JAN 1750
2 ADDR
3 STAE Greater London
3 CTRY UK
1 OCCU Groom or Blacksmith
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas (b.1719) was born in London following his fathers migration there in the early 1700's. A parishoner of St Mary's, Islington and a "free-man of the City of London in the Company of Blacksmiths."  The family's
2 CONC  poverty and misfortune continued and Thomas, a blacksmith died a poor man at the young age of 31.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1750 -- Typhus epidemic sweeps through London, killing thousands including the Lord Mayor. An inquiry traces one possible origin to Newgate Prison, which was "in a very filthy condition and had long been so." This will lead, by 17
2 CONC 79, to John Howard's calls for reform.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1750 -- Gin Lane, an engraving by English artist William Hogarth, helps spur social reform. The engraving depicts a drunken mother surrounded by a scene of squalor. A year later, the Gin Acts give magistrates control over licensin
2 CONC g pubs in Britain. 
