1 NAME Daniel /Willink/
2 GIVN Daniel
2 SURN Willink
2 _MARNM Willink
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC St Michael's in the Hamlet
2 ADDR
3 ADR1  Aigburth
3 CITY Liverpool
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1779
2 ADDR
3 CITY Winterswijk
3 STAE GE
3 CTRY Netherlands
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 JAN 1859
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Aigburth 
3 CITY Liverpool
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU Merchant and Consul for the Netherlands
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Resided in Liverpool (originally London) merchant and Consul for the Netherlands.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Ann[e] Latham 16/03/1808 St Giles Camberwell, when he was shown as of St James Westminster (he was in partnership with Charles Latham and John Abraham Willink in America and England unitl 1819). The couple's daughter Ann w
2 CONC as baptised in London in 1810, but Clara Cecilia was baptised in Liverpool 1816. Death of Daniel Willink of Barnhey near Liverpool in his 80th year, January 1859, leaving £14,000. The evidence of his sons' probates (see nos. 3 and
2 CONC  4 below) suggests some prior in vivo giving by the father.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1807 the assignees of Turnbull, Forbes and Co., convened a meeting of creditors to assent to or dissent from the assignees transferring their rights in La Bonne Intention in Demerara to Mr Daniel Willink in satisfaction of secu
2 CONC rities he then held on other estates and effects of the bankrupts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Willink's great-grandson Sir Henry Urmston Willink (1894-1973), the grandson of Rev. Arthur Willink (1824-62, left £25,000) and son of an architect William Edward Willink (1856-1924), is in the ODNB as politician and academ
2 CONC ic administrator, having served as MP and then Master of Magdalene College.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Willink's son William Williamson Willink formerly of Roby and of Liverpool but late of 3 Hyde Park Gardens left £148,443 11s 2d in 1883. He was described in the 1861 and 1871 censuses as Civil Service - Secty Public Works a
2 CONC nd Secretary Public Works: his wealth at death is hard to square wth his position if the latter was the only source of income.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Willink's daughter Hester married William Robertson Sandbach (q.v), the Liverpool and British Guiana merchant, in 1837.
2 CONT
2 CONT Further Information
2 CONT
2 CONT Wealth at death: £14,000 Occupation: Merchant Associated Claims (1): British Guiana 558 (La bonne intention): £13,378 13S 7D Awardee Details
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacies Summary
2 CONT
2 CONT Commercial (14) Railway Investment: Liverpool and Bury (Bolton, Wigan and Liverpool and Bury Extension) [184598] £5000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: Direct Northern (Lincoln to York) [184537]  £5000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: Cheltenham, Oxford, and London and Birmingham Union; or Charlton Kings and Marsworth [183732] £2000. Other partner: Alpujarras Lead Company Mining  
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: London and Worcester and South Staffordshire (Extension from Dudley and Sedgley Branch) [1845117] £2000. Name partner: Daniel and John Abraham Willink and Co. (North American merchant)
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: London, Worcester and South Staffordshire [1845121] £2000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: Blackburn, Burnley, Accrington and Colne Extension [184514] £2500 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: London and York [1845119] £5000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: London, Worcester and South Staffordshire (Extension from Dudley to Wolverhampton) [1845118] £2000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: Dublin and Belfast Junction (Branch to Kells) [184540] £3500 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: Sheffield and Lincolnshire Junction [1845168]  £5000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: Liverpool, Orm-kirk and Preston [184599*]  £2000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Railway Investment: Lynn and Ely [1845126] £3750 
2 CONT
2 CONT Addresses (2): 3 Goree Piazza, Liverpool, Lancashire, North-west England, England
2 CONT                             61 Rodney Street, Liverpool, Lancashire, North-west England, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
