1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marion (Stonham) Latham was born 14 April, 1861. She married Frederick Nix Latham around 1886 aged 25, Frederick her husband was 3 years younger. They lived in London after marriage where Frederick worked - we beli
2 CONC eve near Greenwich. On 12 June, 1887 she gave birth to Violet Marion Latham, their first child; and on the 17th March, 1889 she gave birth to their second child, a son; Leslie Frederick Latham in Greenwich, London.  When her husba
2 CONC nd retired they moved to Flushing, Falmouth, Cornwall to live in 1908. She did accomplished water colour painting and was a keen gardener. She also travelled to Australia several times , where her two children had moved to live. S
2 CONC he was remembered by her Grand Son, Kenneth (Bunty) Latham as a loving and wonderful woman. She died on 6th April, 1935, aged 73 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Marion (Stonham) Latham was born 14 April, 1861. She married Frederick Nix Latham around 1886 aged 25 years, Frederick her husband was 3 years younger. They lived in London after marriage - we believe near Greenwich , London. On 1
2 CONC 2 June, 1887 she gave birth to Violet Marion Latham, their first child. And on the 17 March, 1889 she gave birth to Leslie Frederick Latham in Greenwich, London. He husband worked in finance in London; either as an Accountant / Br
2 CONC oker / or Banker - maybe with N.M. Rothchild's (?). When her husband retired they moved to Flushing, Falmouth, Cornwall to live in 1908. She did accomplished water colour paintings, was keen at gardening and needlework. She also t
2 CONC raveled to Australia several times to visit her children and grandchildren. She was remembered by her grandson, Keneth (Bunty) Latham as a loving and wonderl woman. She died on 6 April, 1935 aged 73 years in Falmouth, Cornwall.   
2 CONC
