1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Leslie Frederick Latham was the second child of Frederick Nix Latham and Marion (Stonham) Latham. He was born in Greenwich, London. He went to school at Blackfriars School, London. After leaving school he traveled 
2 CONC to Australia for the first time aged 17. He returned to England and attended University at The Camborne School of Mines, University of Exeter Cornwall Campus and studied Mining Engineering from 1908 to 1910 where he graduated as M
2 CONC ining Engineer. Following graduation he left England with the intention of settling in India - but on arrival in India he decided he did not like it so sailed on to Sydney, Australia. After arrival in Australia he found he needed 
2 CONC further education to use his Engineering degree in Australia and elected to attend Agricultural Collage at Wagga Wagga, southern NSW between 1911 and 1912. In 1913 he purchased a 1,200 acre farm at Baan Baa, North West NSW with th
2 CONC e financial assistance of his father in England. On the 5th December 1913 he married Gladys Caroline (Nicholls) Latham in Mosman Anglican Church { Glads born England on 25 March, 1883 and died Wentworth Falls, NSW, Australia on 5 
2 CONC June, 1972 }   Their first born was Desmond Veyvyan Latham (born 8 September 1914. Died 18 February, 2001) Second born was Phillips Stonham Latham (born 22 May, 1916. Killed in Darwin Bombing on 19 February 1942) Third born was Ke
2 CONC nneth Bertram Latham (born 1 April, 1918. Died Bathurst 9 January, 2008) Fourth born was Guy Rodney Latham (born 6 November, 1919 and died Ballina, NSW 2 August, 1997.) Leslie lived on his farm called "Burragurrum" for the rest of
2 CONC  his life. The farm was a wheat and sheep property. His sister Violet had also left England and settled in Box Hill, Melbourne, Australia. She never married and had a female companion. Violet died 2 May, 1970 in Melbourne. Leslie 
2 CONC died of a heart attach aged 74 years - he was in Narribri Hospital. He is buried along side his wife in the cemetery at Baan Baa, Australia.  Leslie Frederick Latham had a reserved, academic nature that was not really suited to fa
2 CONC rming. His nature was some-what lazy, having either a 'share farmer' or his sons work the property most of the time. In his youth he had sailed (membership of the Royal Cornwall Yacht Club), played Rugby and Ice Hockey. On the far
2 CONC m he played tennis, followed the cricket with passion and all his sons were very good at sport. He had skill in craft and made rugs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
