2 CONC e needed further studies to use his Mining Engineer degree and elected to attend Agricultural College at Wagga Wagga, south NSW between 1911 and 1912. In 1913 he purchased a 1,200 acre farm at Baan Baa, North West NSW with the fin
2 CONC ancial assistance of his father in England. On the 5th December 1913 he married Glads Carolyn (Nicholls) Latham in St Luke's Anglican Church, Mosman, NSW {Glads born England on 25 March, 1883 and died Wentworth Falls, NSW, Austral
2 CONC ia on 5 June, 1972.} Their first born child was Desmond Vevyvan Latham (born 8 September, 1914. Died Wahroonga, NSW on 18 February, 2001.) Second born was Phillips Stonham Latham (born 22 May, 1916. Killed in bombing of Darwin; on
2 CONC  19 February, 1942) Third born was Kenneth Bertram Latham (born 01 April, 1918. Died Bathurst, NSW 9 January, 2008). Fourth child born was Guy Rodney Latham (born 6 November, 1919 and died Ballina, NSW 2 August, 1997). Leslie live
2 CONC d on his farm called "Burragurrum" for the rest of his life.The farm was a wheat and sheep property. His sister Violet had also left England and settled in Box Hill, Melbourne, Australia. She never married and had a female compani
2 CONC on (Violet died 2 May, 1970 in Melbourne). Leslie died of a heart attack aged 74 years - he was in Narrabri Hospital, NSW. He is buried , along side his wife in the cemetery at Baan Baa, NSW, Australia. Leslie Frederick had a rese
2 CONC rved, academic nature that was not really suited to farming. His nature was some-what lazy ; either employing a share farmer and later his sons to do much of the work on the farm. His father, Frederick Nix Latham, had provided a T
2 CONC rust Fund to support his livelihood. In his youth he had sailed, being a member of the Royal Cornwall Yacht Club, played Rugby Union and Ice hockey. On the farm he played tennis, followed cricket with passion and all his sons were
2 CONC  good at sport. He had skill in craft making rugs. The family story (English History) had not been passed down by Leslie:- I believe it to be his wife's fault - as Glady's was a very jealous and envious woman and maybe Leslie was 
2 CONC indifferent.    
