1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Violet Marion Latham was the first born child of Frederick Nix Latham and Marion (Stonham) Latham. She was born in Greenwich, London (we think) on 12 June, 1887. It is unknown where she was educated. She was  a ver
2 CONC y good seamstress and loved dogs and gardening. Violet was a tall, slim woman who wore glasses and had a serious (somewhat miserable) manner in her old age as I recall in the 1960's. She was independently wealthy, having the incom
2 CONC e from a Trust Fund given to her by her father, Frederick Nix Latham. She left Flushing, Falmouth and settled in Box Hill, Melbourne, Victoria, Australia at an unknown date, probably after the death of her Mother, Marion in April,
2 CONC  1935. She took with her her 'companion' Agnes (?) with whom it is understood she had a lesbian relationship.  Both Violet and Agnes would visit her brother Leslie Latham and his family on their farm: "Burragurrum", Baan Baa in No
2 CONC rth West NSW (between Boggabri and Narrabri).  I do not know of any work Violet did, or the date of the death of her companion, Agnes - I suspect Agnes died before the 1950's as my generation has no recollection of her.   Violet d
2 CONC ied in Melbourne, Victoria on 2nd May, 1970 aged 82 Years
