1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "That many people now living in South-West Lancashire or elsewhere are descended from the Lathoms of Parbold is certain, although of few indeed could any evidence now he brought of their ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the date of birth of Thomas Lathom of Scarisbrick (25) there is unfortunately no evidence. We know he existed, but know nothing more. But the similarities of time, place, general conditions, and the astonishing repetition of th
2 CONC e Parbold christian names –Edward, Thomas, John and Richard - coupled with the repetition of  “the grandfather’s name, then the father’s“ at precisely the same time and place in the genealogical tree would appear to be too unusual
2 CONC  to be lightly dismissed as just a mere coincidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Be this as it may the fact remains that the only break in the long line of descent from the Founder of Burscough Priory through the younger branches of the Lathom family to the present time (1946) occurs between the children of Ri
2 CONC chard and Elizabeth Lathom (17) and Thomas Lathom of Scarisbrick (25). This single break apart, the genealogical tree is complete, thoroughly established and well documented. In its later phases it comes about in this way.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Lathom of Scarisbrick {25} had four sons - Edward, Thomas, John and Richard, -once more the grandfather’s name, then the father's- baptized at Ormskirk Parish Church in the years 1692, 1694, 1697 and 1699 respectively." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Now three generations after the persecution of the Royalists, the family's misfortunes continued.  Thomas (b.1694) became a coachman and migrated to London in search of a better life.
2 CONT
2 CONT In London, he met and married Margaret Harris on the 2nd of December 1718.  They had at least two children, Thomas and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also http://webspace.webring.com/people/ls/stephhunt/ps02/ps02_041.htm where a Thomas b.1694 had 6 daughters and one son called Richard?
