1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Glads Caroline Nicholls was born in London at 15 Holly Road , Chiswick. She liked to say her year of birth was at least one year later than it was. The Nicholls family migrated to Australia on a windjammer when Gla
2 CONC ds was 2 years old. They settled at “ Camelot “ on Spit Road, Mosman. After school she attended Julian Ashton Art School in Synney along with her sister Muriel (Mops) Nicholls. She married Leslie Frederick Latham on 5th December, 
2 CONC 1913 (year?). Leslie and Glads settled on the Latham farm at “Burragurrum” , Baan Baa, North West NSW. She had four boys .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Glads Caroline (Nicholls) Latham was born in England on 25 March, 1883. In 1884 she sailed with her family on a 'Windjammer' named "Parramatta" to Australia. Glads was the youngest of 5 children ; The others siblings being; Arthur
2 CONC  Nicholls, Violet Nicholls, Marion Nicholls, Herbert Nicholls.  The Nicholls settled at "Camelot", Spit Road, Mosman and her father was a journalist with the Sydney Morning Herald. He later became Sydney Editor for The Argus in Me
2 CONC lbourne and the Australiasian in Melbourne. She attended school in Mosman and studied Art at the Julian Ashton School of Art in Sydney after school. She played the violin and piano. She married Leslie Frederick Latham on 5 Decembe
2 CONC r, 1913 at St. Luke's Anglican Church, Mosman and they had their honeymoon at Caves House, Jenolan Caves, NSW, Australia. Glads and Leslie settled on his farm "Burragurrum" in North West NSW 5 klm out of Baan Baa, on the Narribri 
2 CONC side. They first lived in a small 4 room hut while the homestead was being built. It was completed before the birth of the first child Desmond in 1914. Second child Phillips was born in 1916, third child Kenneth was born 1918, and
2 CONC  fourth child Guy was born 1919. All the children did Correspondence School at home on the farm with the tutelage of their parents. At the earliest age the boys / sons started to work on the family farm. In 1936 Desmond moved to M
2 CONC osman, Sydney to get an education in electrical engineering. The three younger sons joined the Australian Light Horse before the second World War. After the outbreak of war, Desmond, Phillips and Guy all joined the Airforce. Desmo
2 CONC nd became a navigator in NewGuinea and Philipps and Guy moved to Darwin where Phillips was killed in the bombing of Darwin on 19 February, 1942. Kenneth remained on the farm, due to a health judgement, and worked the family farm -
2 CONC  he lived the longest of all the boys so the health issue is a mystery. Glads continued on the farm till about 1969 when she became too aged to live alone after breaking her hip in a fall. At this point she moved to Leura, NSW whe
2 CONC re son Kenneth lived and eventually moved into a nursing home  "Boddington" in Wentworth Falls, NSW next door to Leura in the Blue Mountains where she died on 5th June 1973 aged 89 years. She was a good looking, slim, tough, indep
2 CONC endent  pioneering country woman. She was an exceptionally good shot with her rifle - often providing food for the family with her gun. Her nature was marked by jealousy and being possessive of her 4 handsome sons. She proved her 
2 CONC own worse enemy - being difficult to live with.  
