1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Des served in the RAAF during The Second World War. He was a navigator in Beaufort Bombers in  Papua New Guinea. He meet his future wife Helen Marcia Gilbert who was also in the RAAF. She was in Signals. They got m
2 CONC arried on 27 January, 1943 . Helen was the daughter of John A. Gilbert Group, the first G.M.Holden Car Dealers in NSW  and later Country Bus Lines + Bus Financiers. After the war he worked with an engineering with a manufacturing 
2 CONC group and was an inventor. The family settled in Lindfield on Sydney's North Shore. First child Janece Marcia Latham was born on 2nd May, 1946. Carolyn Latham, the second child was born ---- . After retiring they purchased a 10 ac
2 CONC re farm near Dural and grew trees for nurseries. Later they moved to Bilgola Plateau on the Northern Beaches.
