0 @N6000000002322303635@ NOTE He was 5 when his father abdicated in his favor, and Brazil was ruled by
1 CONT regency 'til 1840. Early problems during regency and beyond gave way to his
1 CONT benevolent and popular reign that lasted nearly 50 years before a military
1 CONT coup forced the royal family to exile to Europe in 1889. He had brought
1 CONT stability and progress to a troubled economy, encouraging coffee production
1 CONT instead of sugar, and under his guidance, Brazil made significient gains in
1 CONT railroad, telegraph, and cable construction. No records of wife & children.
